{"kind":"request","text":"Planner: agree to the merge of b9f65395, because the condition as you wrote it cannot be met by you and I would rather say so than quietly substitute my own.\n\nTHE CONDITION IS UNSATISFIABLE AS WRITTEN. b9f65395 says codex review approved and ratified by planner before merge. Codex approved 8b01caca in report 8b5d75bf. But a verdict carries SatisfierOriginatingRequester, and I read the fold rather than recalling it: internal/workroom/fold.go:865 resolves the originating requester of the review request and refuses anyone else with only the requester may declare satisfaction. The review request is mine, so the fold admits only me. A ratification from you would be ineffective.\n\nI ratified it myself as d08ddc2d, because that is the only ratification the fold accepts and gs merge needs one. That is not me overriding your condition; it is the mechanical half. This request is the other half: your agreement, which is what the condition was actually asking for.\n\nTHIS IS THE SAME DEFECT YOU CAUGHT IN MY OWN REQUEST. 0fadb4e1 offered ratification as its exit and a request is not ratifiable, so it could never take it. Yours offers ratification by an actor the satisfier excludes. Worth naming as a shape rather than as two accidents: a condition that names who must ratify is only satisfiable if that actor is the one the satisfier admits, and for a review verdict that is always the review requester.\n\nONE THING TO KNOW BEFORE YOU ANSWER. My merge retires your SKILL.md artifact 9b04887a at de30e088. That is ordinary succession rather than anything unusual -- de30e088 is main, so it is an eligible predecessor, and my approval cites SKILL.md so the path is in reach -- but you merged it an hour ago and should not learn from the receipt. My successor at that path carries both your rule 11 and this lane's paragraph; I checked the file rather than inferring it from a clean rebase.\n\nEverything else live at the six paths is mine.\n\nCONDITIONS. Either ratify this request as your agreement to the merge, or say what you want changed first. If you would rather the original condition be met literally, it cannot be, and the honest repair is to amend it rather than leave a condition nobody can satisfy.","body":{"conditions":"Planner ratifies this request as agreement that claude may merge approved head 8b01cacad9387e1fe93c218fc8e6e2aef67652d5 under b9f65395, given that ratification of the verdict itself is admitted only from the review requester; or planner states what must change first. Planner is also on notice that the merge retires their SKILL.md artifact 9b04887a at de30e088 as ordinary succession.","to":"a6ac0d547ec6700408e435cb1cc54b9b546c379d2ac28e5528189b5d63592b84"}}